{{ motion_prompt }}

The camera stays a detached third-person observer at a constant distance.
Any camera movement is very slow and minimal.
The colors, white balance, brightness and lighting stay exactly as in the first frame
for the whole shot. No color grading, tint or exposure change.
Every object stays solid and in place: anything a person holds stays in the same hand for the
whole shot, and nothing in the scene appears, disappears or changes shape.
Only the people and objects already in the first frame are in the shot; no one new enters.
{% if dialogue %}
There are exactly {{ dialogue | map(attribute='speaker') | unique | list | length }} different speaking voices in this scene. Each voice is distinct.
The shot opens with about one second of silence. Nobody speaks before the FIRST line below.
{% for line in dialogue %}
{% if line.position -%}
{% if loop.first %}FIRST{% else %}THEN{% endif %}, the person on the {{ line.position }} side of the frame{% if line.look %} ({{ line.look }}){% endif %} speaks{% if line.voice %}. Their voice is {{ line.voice }}{% endif %}.
Only that person's lips move, naturally in sync, as they say in Korean: "{{ line.text }}"
While they speak, everyone else stays silent with their mouth closed.
{% else -%}
{% if loop.first %}FIRST{% else %}THEN{% endif %}, an off-screen voice that is not anyone in the frame speaks (for example through a phone){% if line.voice %}. The voice is {{ line.voice }}{% endif %}.
It says in Korean: "{{ line.text }}"
Nobody in the frame moves their lips for this line; they only listen.
{% endif -%}
{% endfor %}
These are the ONLY words spoken in this shot. Nobody says anything else.
After the last line, everyone closes their mouth and stays completely silent
for the remainder of the shot. Do not invent additional dialogue or chatter
to fill the silence.
{{ mood_line }} No shouting.

{% if solo_side %}The speaker looks toward the other person just outside the frame on the {{ solo_side }} side, never at the camera.
Only this one person is in the frame.{% else %}The speakers look at each other while talking, never at the camera.{% endif %}

Absolutely no subtitles, captions, letters or any on-screen text appear at any time.
Audio: only the Korean lines quoted above, quiet ambient room tone underneath.
No music. No narrator. No background conversation.
{% else %}
{% if listening -%}
The person in the frame is listening to someone who is not in the frame (for example on the phone).
They only listen: their mouth stays closed and their lips never move for the whole shot.
{%- else -%}
The character does not speak and their lips do not move.
{%- endif %}
{{ mood_line }}

Absolutely no subtitles, captions, letters or any on-screen text appear at any time.
{% if ambient -%}
Audio: only the natural sounds of this scene, matching what happens on screen (for example
footsteps, street or cafe ambience, cups and dishes), at a quiet, natural level.
No speech, no voices, no talking in the background, no music.
{%- else -%}
Audio: quiet ambient room tone only. No speech, no dialogue, no music.
{%- endif %}
{% endif %}
